{"id": "DfD3ExHzjcQ", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Why does Shiva’s dance have two names? 🔱🔥 Ananda Tandava is his dance of joy. Rudra Tandava is the fierce one, the dance of destruction.\n\nShiva is Nataraja, the lord of dance, and his tandava has two moods. In the Ananda Tandava he dances in bliss. In the Rudra Tandava he dances as Rudra, the fierce one: the dance that ends a world so that a new one can begin. Tradition remembers his most terrible tandava after Sati gave herself to the fire at Daksha’s yagna.\n\nHere little Mahadev dances the Rudra Tandav: the storm over Kailash, the ring of fire, and his third eye opening on every stomp.\n\nSame dance, same beat as our calm Shiv Tandav. Which one is your Mahadev, calm or Rudra? Tell us below 👇\n\nStories of Shiva, Sati and the gods, written for kids: Rishi Katha books, Books 1–3 as a set for ₹500 at rishikatha.com (link in bio).\n\nFollow @therishikatha for more.\n\n#rudratandav #rudra #shivtandav #mahadev #harharmahadev mahakal nataraja bholenath shiva kailash omnamahshivaya sanatandharma hindu bhakti rishikatha", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1793238542, "like_count": 336, "comment_count": 4, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1139684165590381a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 61.487, "asr": 44100, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr2-2.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQMpP1ZKtGXLNbc0AnIg2FNx_siq1wbPlhXxx1UpZ3JmtSIzaR_fizY2RKapfohjw3IA9B8dZrKu1bcYT7n64cVJrOEWQq6PrBRY0Jw.mp4?_nc_cat=105&_nc_oc=AdqlmvnqvDlec0HZ8EveyDGlmxuTIMEcOjDyWxc8vCKte0Oq9s6MzK_DVQs1ZU0nD4BccgxeHjGwYrdQsFeYqOya&_nc_sid=9ca052&_nc_ht=instagram.fblr2-2.fna.fbcdn.net&_nc_ohc=Hg_0soG69xUQ7kNvwE6lO2K&%3D%3D&ccb=17-1&_nc_gid=oDI8K0Q15l5w71SZ1TxP0w&_nc_ss=70689&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&_nc_zt=28&oh=00_AQRIIJWImDXBDJXtqe9QWUwjLbSC